  "reference_notes": "Compared the Bogdan Giusa and Ryan Hodnett leaf stands, plus Cathy Dewitt winter heads for structural persistence only. Rejected the initial reed-like nodal leaves and replaced them with separate long basal straps and unbranched old head culms. Inspected current small/medium/large pilots and all 36 variants; the open linear leaf fans now read as Typha, 1.10-2.35 m high. Two sparse brown residual heads represent last year rather than fresh spring flowering. Individual head fibres and leaf sheaths remain unresolved at 25 mm. Accepted as a spring wetland-edge cattail source; user seed endorsement remains separate.",
